    <https://schema.org/about> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/dataset/wikimedia-commons-drosophila-compound-eye>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch07-08> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasEvidence> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/cell-geometry-thompson1917-ch07-08>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/cell-geometry-thompson1917-ch07-08> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/EvidenceItem>;
    <https://schema.org/value> "-0.9"^^xsd:double;
    dc:description "Exploratory test of thompson1917-ch07-08: If hexagons are regular only where cells are equal in size, tissues with more uniform cell areas have a larger fraction of six-sided cells, and within a tissue cells in more size-heterogeneous neighbourhoods depart more from six sides.\n\nResult: -0.9 (Spearman rho, tissue area CV vs fraction of six-sided interior cells; n = 5; p = 0.0374).\n\nCriterion: Exploratory, not pre-registered: the images were segmented and inspected before the pass criterion was written. Treat the verdict as hypothesis-generating; a pre-registered replication on new images is needed before it counts as a test. Supports if Spearman rho between tissue area CV and fraction of six-sided interior cells is <= -0.7 across usable tissues; mixed if between -0.7 and 0; refutes if >= 0.\n\nInterpretation: Tests the size-uniformity part only; 'forces uniform' is not measured. This is a second, multi-tissue attempt; the pre-registered within-RPE test of the same claim is test-data/claim-tests/thompson-growth-form/thompson1917-ch07-08/result.json.";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Exploratory, not pre-registered: the images were segmented and inspected before the pass criterion was written. Treat the verdict as hypothesis-generating; a pre-registered replication on new images is needed before it counts as a test.\nOnly 5 tissues; the across-tissue correlation rests on five points.\nThe random-Voronoi control shows the same within-image relation, so the result is a property of space-filling partitions in general and says nothing about forces.";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Exploratory cell-geometry test of thompson1917-ch07-08 on 5 images: supports";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/0d6f11c2931e2a6e86516c68a8e05ad599c76355/test-data/claim-tests/thompson-growth-form/thompson1917-ch07-08/cellpose-multi-tissue/result.json>;
    prov:used <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/dataset/wikimedia-commons-physcomitrella-leaf>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/dataset/wikimedia-commons-festuca-leaf-epidermis>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/dataset/wikimedia-commons-aloe-leaf-epidermis>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/dataset/wikimedia-commons-human-corneal-endothelium>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/dataset/wikimedia-commons-drosophila-compound-eye>;
    <https://schema.org/additionalProperty> sub:value0, sub:value1, sub:value10, sub:value11, sub:value12, sub:value13, sub:value14, sub:value15, sub:value16, sub:value17, sub:value18, sub:value19, sub:value2, sub:value20, sub:value21, sub:value3, sub:value4, sub:value5, sub:value6, sub:value7, sub:value8, sub:value9;
    <https://schema.org/unitText> "Spearman rho, tissue area CV vs fraction of six-sided interior cells";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/pValue> "0.0374"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/statisticalTest> "Spearman rank correlation across 5 tissues, two-sided"
}
